Indeed, the way skills work for spell casting needs
a major overhaul at some point.  There are a small
number of spells for which it makes a big difference
irrespective of failure rate, and there are likewise
a couple of high-level spells that you need skill to
get a decent failure rate on; but neither of these
situations is even remotely common for most roles.
(Wizard is the main role that both tends to want to 
use spells in these categories and also has access
to the skill; and to a lesser extent also Monk and 
perhaps in some cases Priest.)  There are also a
couple of roles that can benefit from divination
skill in the early or early-mid game, purely for
the improved failure rate on identify, if they
happen to get that spell early.

Which roles have access to which skills is also
rather arbitrary.  dtsund has written a proposal 
that would make some improvements in this regard,
but that still leaves the problem of skills not
DOING anything particularly useful for most spells 
for most roles.  Something akin to ais523's wand
skill proposal, but for spells, might be needed.

